@prefix : <http://example.org/trust-domain/decision-cases#> .
@prefix dm: <http://example.org/trust-domain/decision#> .
@prefix td: <http://example.org/trust-domain#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

# Insider branch B: the trusts are not disqualified persons.
# The only facts that make this consistent: the foundation holds the whole
# beneficial interest of the family trust, the family holds none, and the
# business trust's beneficial interest flows through the family trust to the
# foundation (4946(a)(4), 267(c)). The family trust must also not be a
# substantial contributor (4946(a)(1)(A)) unless it is itself treated as a
# 501(c)(3) organization (4947(a)(1)), which 53.4946-1(a)(8) excludes from the
# disqualified-person list for 4941 only. Not legal advice.

dm:BranchNotInsiders dm:selectedBy "tests/decision/branch-b.ttl" .

# No disqualified-person facts for the trusts or the operating company here.
# The stress-case trust still passes value to a family member (decision-cases.ttl),
# which the hack test catches (H2).

# P14: 4943(d)(1) now treats the business trust's 30 percent as the foundation's
# own, through the trust chain: 15 bought + 30 attributed = 45. The 4947(a)(2)
# remainder exception does not apply to a trust that is not split-interest.
:P14_OperatingCoShares dm:foundationVotingPercentAfter "45"^^xsd:decimal ;
    dm:disqualifiedVotingPercent "0"^^xsd:decimal .
